<title>USA: Premiere Radio sets stock buyback.</title>
<headline>Premiere Radio sets stock buyback.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Premiere Radio Networks Inc said Friday it planned to buy back $3.0 million of its common shares from time to time in the open market or through negotiated transactions.</p>
<p>The company has about $20.0 million in cash and no long-term debt, it said.</p>
<p>Premiere Radio shares were trading recently at 10-1/2.</p>
<p>The company has about 3.6 million common shares and 4.0 million Class A shares outstanding.</p>
</text>
